oken.\" Means we assume prediction_tokens >= 1. But if zero, we could raise ValueError? It says \"Raise ValueError for an infeasible or structurally invalid case\". I'll assume prediction_tokens >= 1. If not, we should raise ValueError? The task says \"Do not mutate the input. All ranking and traversal ties use the source position or identifier specified above; never depend on hash-map iteration.\" So we'll keep order as in list.\n\nImplementation: define solve(case): get threshold = case['threshold'], calls = case['calls']. For each call in calls, compute gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call, normalized = gain / prediction_tokens. accepted = call['parseable'] and normalized >= threshold. Append to diagnostics dict. Build accepted_call_ids from accepted ones.\n\nReturn dict.\n\nNeed to ensure we don't mutate case.\n\nWrite Python code.\n\nAlso, the solve function must be named solve and take case argument.\n\nWe'll return the result.\n\nNow produce the JSON response with key \"implementation\" containing the Python source as a JSON-escaped string.\n\nLet's write code."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":2164,"completion_tokens":1083,"total_tokens":3247,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":2048},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":834},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":2048,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":116},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}